# The K-quant kernel's decode variant in llama.cpp's shape: block reads along K

# Applied against the pinned runtime, build 2026.4.0-22849-71640275d29, on top of
# patches/0003-0022. arcint 0.4.1 (DESIGN.md section 7.0.2bc). Replaces the earlier 0023
# (the timing test only), which is carried inside this one.
#
# What changes:
#   fully_connected_gpu_kquant.cl   The decode variant (TILE_M == 1): a work-group per
#                       group of output rows (KQ_ROWS: four, sixteen on the long-K down
#                       projection), KQ_WG = 4 subgroups with their lanes along K, a subgroup
#                       taking one super-block per iteration; super-blocks outer, rows inner,
#                       so the activation super-block is read once (a sub-group block read,
#                       converted once) and shared by the rows; the subgroups' partials
#                       reduced through local memory. The tiled prefill variant is unchanged.
#   kquant_utils.cl     The row pieces. Q4_K/Q5_K (kq_row_q4k_x): the 128 quant bytes as one
#                       intel_sub_group_block_read_uc8 -- lane l holds positions l and l + 16
#                       of every sub-block -- the eight scale/min pairs decoded by lanes 0..7
#                       and broadcast, the min term from the activation pair sums. Q6_K
#                       (kq_row_q6k_x): the 2-aligned 210-byte blocks block-read as dwords
#                       from the dword at or below the block and redistributed with one
#                       shuffle (a 16-bit block read two bytes off a dword returns the wrong
#                       word on every lane but the first -- measured), the scales one uniform
#                       load; on Xe2 the subgroup prefetches its next Q6_K super-block (one
#                       cache line per lane: the Q6_K down projection 500 -> 397 us on the 24 GB
#                       card, measured; the Q4_K/Q5_K shapes and the 16 GiB card lose with the
#                       same prefetch and do not get it). Q8_0 per lane. Exact: f32 accumulation
#                       over f16 activations.
#   fully_connected_kernel_kquant.cpp   The decode dispatch: a work-group of 4 x 16 lanes per
#                       rows_per_group(K) output rows; KQ_ROWS and KQ_PREFETCH (Xe2) as jit
#                       constants; the subgroup reduce among the required device features. The
#                       width-sized K split of 0022 goes.
#   fully_connected_gpu_test.cpp   Two more correctness cases (Q8_0 and Q5_K at one row); the
#                       timing case streams (eight weight buffers in rotation on one queue: ten
#                       launches of one buffer had let a third of it hit L2), warms every network
#                       to steady state before the clock (a network's second execution costs
#                       twice its third, measured) and runs over the served model's own tensor
#                       types and shapes.
#
# MEASURED streamed at steady state on the 24 GB card, one row, against 0022 in the same
# instrument: the gate projection (Q4_K, N 17,408, K 5,120) 141 us / 355 GB/s (79 % of the
# card's measured 453 GB/s random-read ceiling) against 170; the Q4_K down projection
# (N 5,120, K 17,408) 146 against 219; Q5_K 5,120 x 5,120 60 against 137; the Q6_K down
# projection 397 against 646; the N 1,024 projections 20-33 us. Served (dense Qwen3.8-27B
# Q4_K_M native, u8 KV): 12.1 t/s decode at 856 prompt tokens against 0.4.0's 9.9, 10.1 at
# 71.7k against 8.5, Pruefstand 10/10, greedy outputs byte-identical at both depths. DESIGN
# 7.0.2bc-7.0.2bd.
#
# Upstream: not yet filed.

